\\012\\012- [ ] All \"must have\" requirements addressed\\012- [ ] Success metrics achievable with implementation\\012- [ ] No PRD sections left unimplemented\\012- [ ] Dependencies correctly handled\\012\\012## Simplification\\012\\012Hunt actively for simplification — do not just tick boxes. The diff under\\012review is fresh; this is the cheapest moment to cut complexity before it sets.\\012For every added or changed file, ask \"what would make this simpler to read\\012without changing what it does?\" and flag concrete opportunities.\\012\\012- [ ] **Reduce complexity** — no needless indirection, dead branches, or\\012      abstractions built for a single caller; nesting <= 4 levels; functions\\012      under 50 lines\\012- [ ] **Eliminate redundancy** — no logic duplicated within the diff or against\\012      existing code; no helper that reimplements a stdlib or existing utility\\012- [ ] **Improve naming** — names state intent; no opaque abbreviations;\\012      action-named functions start with a verb\\012- [ ] **Follow project standards** — conventions from CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md and\\012      the surrounding code; no style drift\\012- [ ] **No dead code** — no commented-out blocks, unused imports, variables, or\\012      speculatively-added parameters\\012- [ ] **Appropriate error handling** — explicit, never silently swallowed\\012\\012**How to flag a simplification:** give the file:line, the current shape, and\\012the simpler replacement. Flag concrete behavior-preserving simplifications at\\012🟡 Medium so the decision gate routes them into the rework loop. Do not inflate\\012them to 🟠 High; that floods the rework loop and can trip the scope alarm.\\012\\012**Balance — do not over-simplify:** never propose a change that trades clarity\\012for brevity, drops error handling, collapses a deliberate boundary, or removes\\012a documented invariant. Simpler means easier to read and maintain, not shorter\\012at any cost. If a \"simplification\" would change behavior, it is out of scope —\\012do not flag it.\\012\\012## Testing\\012\\012- [ ] Unit tests for new logic\\012- [ ] Edge cases covered\\012- [ ] Error paths tested\\012- [ ] Integration tests if crossing boundaries\\012- [ ] Tests actually run and pass\\012- [ ] No tautological test — every new or changed test fails against the\\012      pre-change code (the context's fail-first replay block), and no assert\\012      is constant, self-comparing, or an either-or hedge (the shapes block)\\012\\012## Security\\012\\012- [ ] No hardcoded secrets\\012- [ ] Input validation at boundaries\\012- [ ] No SQL/command injection risks\\012- [ ] Auth/authz correctly applied\\012- [ ] Sensitive data not logged\\012\\012## Documentation\\012\\012- [ ] Public APIs documented\\012- [ ] Complex logic has comments\\012- [ ] README updated if needed\\012- [ ] Breaking changes noted\\012\\012In addition, work through the numbered rubric:\\012# Review-Work-Completion Rubric\\012\\012This rubric defines binary pass/fail criteria for consensus review of completed work. Each rule is numbered and stable for tracking coverage. Reviewers must answer \"R{n}: pass|fail\" for every rule in their prompt.\\012\\012## Rules\\012\\012### Tests\\012\\012R1: Tests cover every new behavior introduced by the diff.\\012R2: Tests bind to intent, not just observable behavior; no new or changed test is tautological (passes against the pre-change code, or cannot fail as written).\\012R3: No skipped or xfail tests mask failures.\\012\\012### Integration\\012\\012R4: Changed components integrate with existing callers.\\012\\012### Security\\012\\012R6: No hardcoded secrets in the codebase.\\012R7: All user input is validated and sanitized.\\012R8: No injection-unsafe queries or commands.\\012\\012### Domain\\012\\012R9: Implementation matches PRD feature behavior exactly.\\012R10: Error handling is explicit and not swallowed.\\012R11: No debug statements, TODOs, or placeholder markers remain.\\012\\012### Code Quality\\012\\012R12: Function sizes respect the 50-line limit.\\012R13: File sizes respect the 800-line limit.\\012\\012Review the completed work against PRD requirements. Explore the codebase as needed.\\012\\012OUTPUT FORMAT IS MANDATORY. Follow exactly:\\012## Agent Output Format (Single Source of Truth)\\012\\012Each agent outputs issues in this exact format:\\012\\012```\\012[{AGENT_NAME}] {emoji} {description} | File: {path or \"N/A\"} | Task: {id or \"general\"}\\012```\\012\\012**Severity emojis:** 🔴 Critical, 🟠 High, 🟡 Medium, ⚪ Low\\012\\012**Rules:**\\012- One issue per line\\012- Use \"N/A\" for file if issue is architectural/cross-cutting\\012- Use \"general\" for task if issue spans multiple tasks or is a PRD gap\\012- If zero issues found: `[{AGENT_NAME}] ✅ No issues found`\\012\\012**Examples:**\\012```\\012[ALICE] 🔴 SQL injection in query builder | File: src/db/query.ts | Task: 3\\012[BOB] 🟠 Missing error handling strategy | File: N/A | Task: general\\012[CARL] 🟡 PRD section 2.3 not implemented | File: N/A | Task: 5\\012```\\012\\012Your agent name is CARL.\\012\\012Cite files repo-relative as path:line (for example skills/work/SKILL.md:166), never absolute and never with a \"(lines a-b)\" suffix.\\012\\012PER-RULE VERDICTS ARE MANDATORY. For every rule in the numbered rubric, emit one line:\\012R{n}: pass   or   R{n}: fail\\012(one rule per line, no other text on the line, no rationale).\\012\\012## Frontend & Design Focus\\012\\012You still review every dimension in the checklist, but you are the panel's\\012frontend and design specialist. On any UI, component, styling, or\\012user-facing change, review with extra depth:\\012\\012- Accessibility: semantic markup, keyboard navigation, focus management,\\012  ARIA usage, colour contrast, screen-reader labels.\\012- Responsive behaviour: layout across breakpoints, overflow, touch targets.\\012- Visual consistency: design-token usage, spacing/typography scale, reuse\\012  of existing components over one-off styling.\\012- UX correctness: loading/empty/error states, form validation feedback,\\012  no layout shift, sensible defaults.\\012- Component structure: state vs props boundaries, no prop drilling,\\012  composability, no duplicated markup.\\012\\012If the change has no frontend surface, review it as a generalist against\\012the shared checklist - do not invent frontend findings.\n31402     1 52-03:09:16 /Applications/eM Client.app/Contents/MacOS/eM Client\n31403     1 52-03:09:15 /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/SafariPlatformSupport.framework/Versions/A/XPCServices/com.apple.SafariPlatformSupport.Helper.xpc/Contents/MacOS/com.apple.SafariPlatformSupport.Helper\n31497     1 01-03:21:25 /Applications/Claude.app/Contents/MacOS/Claude\n31520     1 01-03:21:23 /Applications/Claude.app/Contents/Frameworks/Electron Framework.framework/Helpers/chrome_crashpad_handler --no-rate-limit --monitor-self-annotation=ptype=crashpad-handler --database=/Users/bob/Library/Application Support/Claude/Crashpad --url=https://f.a.k/e --annotation=_productName=Claude --annotation=_version=2.42304.0 --annotation=plat=OS X --annotation=prod=Electron --annotation=ver=44.7.2 --handshake-fd=16\n31523 31497 01-03:21:23 /Applications/Claude.app/Contents/Frameworks/Claude Helper.app/Contents/MacOS/Claude Helper --type=gpu-process --user-data-dir=/Users/bob/Library/Application Support/Claude --gpu-preferences=WAAAAAAAAAAgAQAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAGAAQAAAAAAAAAADAAAAAAAAADgAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKAAAAAAAAAAoAAAAAAAAAAgAAAAAAAAADAAAAAEAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAgAAAAAAAAACAAAAAAAAAA= --shared-files --field-trial-handle=1718379636,r,14608088721575737830,3951134875175560572,262144 --enable-features=DocumentPolicyIncludeJSCallStacksInCrashReports,IsolatesPriorityUseProcessPriority,PdfUseShowSaveFilePicker,ScreenCaptureKitPickerScreen,ScreenCaptureKitStreamPickerSonoma --disable-features=ConnectionAllowlists,DropInputEventsWhilePaintHolding,LocalNetworkAccessChecks,ScreenAIOCREnabled,SpareRendererF