+{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor p in ['docs/dev/project-management/prds/wip/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1.md','docs/dev/project-management/designs/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1-design.md','docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/reports/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1-implementation-models.md']:\n print('\\\\nFILE',p); print(Path(p).read_text())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"\nFILE docs/dev/project-management/prds/wip/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1.md\n---\ncatchup: run\ndesign: run\nrework_cap: 2\ndefault_model: opus\nmodel_tier_rationale: stable identity for ID-less observations and bounded presentation require designed behavior\n---\n\n# Faithful recent activity display\n\n## Overview\n\n### Problem Statement\n\n[PRD 00009 review 2](../../reviews/00009-codex-adapter-v1-review-2.md) R3 shows\nreal provisional errors/warnings lose detail and are overwritten by unrelated\nID-less turn messages. R10 hides recent work behind old activity and lanes.\nR27 tests invented input payloads, while R11 documents obsolete fixture/display\nbehavior. Repair these shared-model presentation defects under the\n[resolved discovery](../../discovery/00001-ovcaq-v1.md).\nPremise: recheck each defect before changing code; already-correct behavior gets\nregression coverage and an explicit skip, never a forced rewrite.\n\n### Target Users\n\nOperators watching current tool activity and failure details in live or plain TUI.\n\n### Success Metrics\n\nDecoder-produced errors, warnings, tools and plans render accurate detail;\nunrelated ID-less records remain distinct; the latest activity appears first.\nRetained model history stays bounded at the existing MAX_ACTIVITY limit.\n\n## Functional Decomposition\n\n### Capability: Accurate activity projection\n\n#### Feature: Actual payload details and identities\n- **Description**: Project native adapters' real normalized payloads faithfully.\n- **Inputs**: activity.message records with text or detail, with or without a\n  nonblank message_id; real normalized tool and plan records.\n- **Outputs**: Existing ActivityItem records in the shared ProjectView.\n- **Behavior**: Use text when present, otherwise detail. Real message IDs update\n  their existing item; absent/blank IDs identify distinct observed records so a\n  turn marker cannot replace an error. Repeated snapshots must not duplicate\n  already-consumed records. Preserve existing eviction, reset and bounds.\n  Remove the invented tool input fallback and use actual driver output in tests.\n\n### Capability: Recent activity presentation\n\n#### Feature: Bounded recent window\n- **Description**: Keep the current activity visible with large retained histories.\n- **Inputs**: ProjectView activity and lane histories.\n- **Outputs**: Rich Activity panel used by live and plain rendering.\n- **Behavior**: Render the newest 20 activity entries first, newest first; then\n  at most 20 lanes in their existing order. State how many entries/lanes were\n  omitted when nonzero. This display limit does not truncate retained models or\n  change lifecycle policy. Preserve existing text sanitization and empty states.\n  The fixed window is this repair's explicit UI policy, requiring no user choice\n  during implementation and no new configuration surface.\n\n#### Feature: Current fixture and display documentation\n- **Description**: Make operator/fixture documentation match checked-in evidence.\n- **Inputs**: Existing lanes-matched.jsonl and actual normalized activity behavior.\n- **Outputs**: Updated fixture matrix, driver protocol and changelog.\n- **Behavior**: Document matched-lane fixture truthfully; remove the obsolete\n  in-place variant and lanes-only claims. Describe tools/messages/plans, detail\n  fallback, and the recent window without claiming real provider smoke evidence.\n\n## Structural Decomposition\n\n### Repository Structure\n\n```text\nsrc/ovcaq/tui/{model.py,panels.py}\ntests/tui/test_activity_projection.py    # new behavioral regressions\ntests/tui/test_activity_window.py        # new renderer regressions\ntests/tui/test_rework_activity.py        # replace invented payload assertion\ntests/fixtures/README.md\ndocs/driver-protocol.md\nCHANGELOG.md\n```\n\n### Module: Activity model\n- **Maps to capability**: Accurate activity projection.\n- **Responsibility**: Shared normalized projection and real-payload regression coverage.\n- **Exports**: Existing ProjectObserver, ProjectView and ActivityItem; no new public API.\n\n### Module: Activity presentation\n- **Maps to capability**: Recent activity presentation.\n- **Responsibility**: Bounded renderer, renderer tests, fixture/protocol documentation\n  and user-facing changelog.\n- **Exports**: Existing activity_panel; no provider-specific code in TUI.\n\n## Dependency Graph\n\n### Foundation Layer (Phase 0)\n- **Activity model**: Existing normalized event records and bounded shared observer.\n\n### Core Layer (Phase 1)\n- **Activity presentation**: Depends on Activity model.\n\n### Integration Layer (Phase 2)\n- **Documentation and conformance**: Depends on Activity model and Activity presentation.\n- Execute after 00051–00053 repairs; preserve their terminal and safety semantics.\n\n## Implementation Phases\n\n### Phase 0: Foundation\n**Goal**: Preserve correct message detail and identity through projection.\n\n**Tasks**:\n- [ ] Repair projection and actual-shape tests (no deps). Acceptance: `uv run\n  pytest tests/tui/test_activity_projection.py tests/tui/test_rework_activity.py`\n  exercises both adapters' decoded payloads, repeated ID-less errors followed by\n  turn markers, real-ID updates, repeated snapshots, eviction and observer reset.\n\n**Exit Criteria**: Error detail survives unrelated later events without duplicates.\n\n### Phase 1: Core\n**Goal**: Put current activity at the top of bounded output.\n\n**Tasks**:\n- [ ] Render the recent window (depends on: Phase 0). Acceptance: `uv run pytest\n  tests/tui/test_activity_window.py` asserts newest activity precedes lanes,\n  exact 20-entry/20-lane limits, omission counts, empty states, safe text and\n  unchanged retained ProjectView history through Rich Console text capture.\n\n**Exit Criteria**: Live/plain Activity content has deterministic bounded entries.\n\n### Phase 2: Integration\n**Goal**: Align documentation with actual fixtures and final display behavior.\n\n**Tasks**:\n- [ ] Correct fixture matrix, protocol and changelog (depends on: Phase 1).\n  Acceptance: documents name lanes-matched.jsonl, actual activity and the 20/20\n  window; obsolete in-place variant and lanes-only assertions are absent.\n\n**Exit Criteria**: `uv sync --all-groups`, `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check .`,\n`uv run ruff format --check .`, `uv run mypy src/ovcaq` and `uv build` pass.\nRun all mandatory review lenses in a fresh session after build handoff.\n\n## Test Strategy\n\n### Critical Scenarios\n- **Happy path**: Tools with true IDs update one entry and display current state.\n- **Edge case**: ID-less warning/error/turn messages remain distinct at the cap.\n- **Error case**: Controls and synthetic credentials cannot appear unsanitized;\n  arbitrary unknown shapes retain tolerant existing handling.\n\n## Risks\n\n- **Duplicate replay**: Use actual observer cursor semantics rather than random IDs.\n- **Hidden history**: Omission counts make the display window explicit; raw evidence\n  and retained model data are unchanged.\n- **Scope**: No lifecycle decisions in TUI, new configuration, historical test\n  renaming, fixture relabeling or real provider calls.\n\n\nFILE docs/dev/project-management/designs/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1-design.md\n# Faithful recent activity design\n\n## Architecture fit\n\nRepair normalized observation projection and Rich presentation in the existing TUI boundary. No provider decoding, lifecycle, persisted schema or public API changes. PRDs 00051–00053 are complete; preserve their safety and terminal behavior.\n\n## Module placement\n\nEdit `src/ovcaq/tui/model.py` and `tests/tui/test_rework_activity.py`; add `tests/tui/test_activity_projection.py`. Edit `src/ovcaq/tui/panels.py`; add `tests/tui/test_activity_window.py`. Update `tests/fixtures/README.md`, `docs/driver-protocol.md` and `CHANGELOG.md`.\n\n## Interfaces & contracts\n\n### Projection\n\nKeep `ProjectObserver._observe_activity(self, event: Observation) -> None`, `ActivityItem` and `ProjectView.activity` unchanged. For `ObservationType.ACTIVITY_MESSAGE`, use `payload['text']` when not None (including empty text), otherwise `payload.get('detail')`; plans continue to summarize `items`. A nonblank string `message_id` updates its existing item using the exact original ID as an internal key. IDs must not be sanitized or truncated for identity; displayed values still pass through `display_text`. Absent, blank or non-string IDs identify distinct consumed records using an observer-local monotonic counter and a separate key namespace. Reset that counter in `_clear()` with activity. `JsonlFollower` delivers each appended record once; do not add content deduplication or random IDs. Repeated polls without new records retain exactly the same items. Preserve re-insertion ordering, eviction at `MAX_ACTIVITY`, session changes and follower reset semantics. Tools use `detail` only; remove the invented `input` fallback. Keep existing plan, literal text and credential sanitization.\n\n### Presentation\n\nKeep `activity_panel(view: ProjectView) -> Panel` and its shared live/plain callers. Render `reversed(view.activity[-20:])` first; then `view.lanes[:20]` in existing order. If activity length exceeds 20 append a literal count line `<n> activity entries omitted`; if lanes length exceeds 20 append `<n> lanes omitted`. Keep `no lanes observed` when lanes are empty and preserve the empty activity behavior. Never mutate or truncate either retained tuple. Pass all dynamic values through existing `display_text` and literal `_panel` Text rendering. No new configuration.\n\n### Documentation\n\nDescribe `lanes-matched.jsonl` as checked-in matched-lane evidence. Remove obsolete in-place variant and lanes-only claims. Describe actual normalized tools/messages/plans, text/detail precedence and the newest-first 20 activity plus at most 20 lanes window. Do not claim live provider smoke evidence. Add the user-visible correction to the existing Unreleased changelog section.\n\n## Data flow\n\nNative drivers produce normalized observations; the existing follower cursor feeds only new records into the observer. Real IDs update, ID-less records append, and bounded retained items become immutable ProjectView tuples. Both live and plain renderers consume the same panel with a smaller presentation window. Raw evidence remains unchanged.\n\n## Reuse inventory\n\nSearches `render|project|observe` and `identity|message|activity|cursor` found `src/ovcaq/tui/model.py:ProjectObserver._apply`, `_observe_activity`, `_clear`, `display_text`; reuse cursor/reset and sanitization. `src/ovcaq/events/tail.py:JsonlFollower` already handles record offsets, replacement and truncation; no new replay tracker. `src/ovcaq/tui/panels.py:_panel` already uses literal Rich Text; retain it. `tests/tui/model_support.py:Projection` and `tests/tui/test_model.py:projection` supply observer fixtures. Existing driver decode tests and checked-in native fixtures supply real normalized payloads.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n1. Smallest diff: add detail fallback and a consumed-record counter in the observer, slice tuples only in the panel. Chosen: fixes identity without a new event protocol or persisted data.\n2. Hash payload/timestamp for anonymous IDs: rejected because identical separately observed errors must remain distinct.\n3. Add native IDs or cursor fields to normalized records: rejected as unnecessary provider/event schema work outside scope.\n\n## Risks & edge cases\n\nEmpty text wins over detail; blank IDs do not update. Anonymous keys must not collide with real IDs. Long IDs sharing sanitized prefixes remain distinct. File/session resets clear counters and history together, avoiding replay duplicates. MAX_ACTIVITY bounds retained memory; the counter stores only one integer. Future configurable windows can replace constants without changing models; future pagination can read retained tuples; future decoder shapes remain provider edge work. No durable state changes require migration or rollback; ordinary git revert restores presentation behavior.\n\n## Test strategy outline\n\nIndependent decoder-to-observer regressions for both adapters, provisional errors/warnings followed by turn markers, repeated identical ID-less records, actual tools/plans, real-ID updates, repeated polls with a real follower, eviction and reset. Rich Console captures verify 20/20 counts/order, omission lines, exact boundaries, literal/safe text, empty states and unchanged retained views. Recheck premises before edits; correct behavior receives coverage and an explicit skip. Run the full documented quality suite once after all tasks.\n\n## Review log\n\ndispatch 1 (claude): cardinal-sin 0, blocker 0, non-blocker 1, question 1\nHost mapping: fresh native OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol/high; engagement retry completed with anchored checks. Source token `claude` is a compatibility label only. Non-blocker: Architecture fit incorrectly says 00051–00053 complete; 00052 remains held and is not a prerequisite. Question: exact original ID means the normalized payload ID; upstream sanitization cannot be undone. Verified cursor/reset, anonymous namespace, text/detail precedence, ordering/window, sanitization, resource bounds and checked-in fixture truth.\n\ndispatch 2 (codex): cardinal-sin 0, blocker 0, non-blocker 5, question 3\nHost mapping: external Anthropic Sonnet/high through real use-sonnet wrapper; source `codex` token is a compatibility label only. Raw findings: `docs/dev/tmp/00054-design-review-2-output.txt`. Non-blockers: explicitly identify the existing bounded key dictionary; pin omitted counts to length minus 20; constrained live height may clip lower rows; clarify existing reinsertion ordering; prerequisite wording. Questions: session identity reset; malformed text/detail and missing key behavior; explicit skip means no production rewrite plus regression coverage. These are recorded without changing design per the source non-blocker/question rule. Existing `_activity` dict is the sole index and evicts keys/items together, and `_clear` clears it on session/reset; preserve those existing behaviors. No open cardinal sins or blockers. Dispatch 2 has section-anchored evidence and more than three findings; no engagement retry or dispatch 3 required.\n\n\nFILE docs/dev/project-management/autopilot/reports/00054-activity-projection-corrections-v1-implementation-models.md\n# Implementation model audit\n\n- Task 1: tess-1, session 01a13c02-db36-72f2-9e0b-bba8f8d1579e, models ['gpt-6.1-sol', 'gpt-6.1-sol', 'gpt-6.1-sol', 'gpt-6.1-sol']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 1: ivan-1, session 01a13c14-48d2-79b1-8468-7dd055d07284, models ['gpt-6.1-sol']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 1: ivan-1-repair, session 01a13c16-a6c9-7180-85b0-fc5ef5b43fe5, models ['gpt-6-astra']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 1: task-1-harness-repair, session 01a13bfc-7cda-77e1-a993-9778c7536d9b, models ['gpt-6.1-sol']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 2: tess2, session 01a13f81-81fa-7d32-8e43-61499609ab6f, models ['gpt-6.1-sol', 'gpt-6.1-sol']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 2: ivan2, session 01a13f86-37d0-7ea2-a565-6a5eddca6956, models ['gpt-6.1-sol']; observed turn_context rows, provider from session_meta.\n- Task 2: ivan2_status, session 01